course: dictionary
lesson: 4915
title: Immediately: at once, or right next to
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The word immediately has two main meanings. The first is at once, right now, without waiting. «If there is a fire alarm, leave immediately.» You do not stop to finish your game or find your coat. You go.
explain: The second meaning is directly next to something, with nothing in between. «The shed is immediately behind the school.» Here immediately tells you the shed is right at the back, not a little way off. Ask yourself: is there a waiting or a time question? Then it means at once. Is there a place question? Then it means right next to.
explain: In a story, immediately can show what happens straight after something else. «Immediately after the bell, the children ran out.» The word links two events closely in time. In British English, immediately can also work like as soon as: «Immediately the bell rang, the children ran out.»
fact: Immediately means at once, right now, without waiting.
fact: Immediately can also mean directly next to, with nothing in between: «immediately behind the school».
fact: «Immediately» is an adverb in «leave immediately» and «call immediately».
fact: In British English, «immediately» can be a conjunction meaning as soon as: «Immediately the bell rang, we ran.»
fact: In safety instructions, «immediately» means no delay: «tell an adult immediately» means tell them now.
exercise: «The fire alarm rang, so the teacher said, leave immediately.» What does immediately mean here? | Later, after lunch | *At once, with no waiting | Quietly, so nobody notices | Slowly, after you finish your drink
exercise: «Here and there wicked little faces popped out of holes, but vanished immediately at sight of the valorous animal.» What does vanished immediately mean? | Slowly walked away | Came back later | *Disappeared at once | Grew bigger
exercise: «The shed is immediately behind the school.» Which meaning of immediately fits? | At once, without waiting | Far away | Long ago | *Right next to, with nothing in between
test: «If you swallow something poisonous by mistake, tell an adult immediately.» Which word in this sentence means without delay? | poisonous | tell | *immediately | adult
test: Which word means as soon as, in «Immediately the bell rang, the children ran out»? | Until | Before | Because | *As soon as
exam: Which word means at once, with no delay? | Curt | Barely | Ancient | *Immediately
